{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1344641-lancea-et-sanctum-in-the-crusades","id":1344641,"title":"Lancea et Sanctum in the Crusades","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-30T05:56:10-07:00","id":1344641,"title":"Lancea et Sanctum in the Crusades","content":"Preparing just the final touches for my Vampire Dark Ages game and I wanted to ask some tips about the Lancea et Sanctum. They are firmly placed in the Holy Lands, Kingdom of Jerusalem to be precise, and I wanted to ask some tips about how to flesh them. They are the dominant power in the PC's city, the Prince is the Archbishop and everyone has a different idea on what to do during the Crusades, with the caveat that Jerusalem must be taken back and fast. I'm starting with some personal troubles before putting them in a turf war with the emerging Circle of the Crone. What would exactly Kindred do after being embraced, though? When should I dump some information about the situation? How present should their sires be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T04:00:19-07:00","id":1344887,"title":"","content":"Check out the Al-Hamasoun Covenant from Dark Eras Companion. The Islamic counterpart to the Lancea et Sanctum.<br /> <br /> Also, which Crusade were you talking about? There were like nine of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T08:45:16-07:00","id":1344951,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think you need to specify the timeframe. It looks like you're after 1187 (reconquest of Jerusalem by Saladin) at least.<br /> <br /> One key point to consider is the impact of the siege of Jerusalem in 1099. That event was marked with excessive blood-letting and frenzy on the part of the mortal knights... so what was going on amongst the Kindred of the city and the crusading camps? WHY did things fall out as they did? --Jerusalem was noteworthy for its excesses, almost in echo of the city's fall to the Romans in AD70.<br /> <br /> Can you draw occulted parallels between these events, and how?<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. The Circle of the Crone was not formalized as such during this time--that comes much, MUCH later. What you have, however, are a hodgepodge of smaller cult frameworks that have something <i>similar</i> to Cruac, without perhaps some of the formalization that eventually emerges.<br /> <br /> It's not quite as simple as &quot;Circle with the serial numbers filed off&quot;, but it can be mechanically the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T13:20:47-07:00","id":1345317,"title":"","content":"In the WoD, Malkav caused the bloodlust in 1099 when Jerusalem fell. Maybe something similar happened in the CoD universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T13:36:54-07:00","id":1345319,"title":"","content":"Might check out the old Ancient Mysteries and Ancient bloodlines books, they were sort of Dark Eras before Dark Eras and one time period covered was during the Crusades.<br /> <br /> 'Clash of Empires: The Crusades (CE 1095-1300): The Camarilla fell, and the Invictus and the Lancea Sanctum were the powers in Europe\u2019s nights. But there were other covenants then, as well, and in this flash point we see their rise and fall.'<br /> <br /> Here's an excerpt, 'The Lancea+Sanctum never had a knack for widespread rule, and with a booming Kindred population and a disease-ravaged mortal populace, Lancea+Sanctum archbishops often found themselves stepping aside for more politically astute Kindred to rule in their stead. These Kindred lords were often anointed Sanctified themselves, but were rarely of the studious nature necessary to become a frocked member of the priesthood. As a result, many of these princes considered themselves only nominally Sanctified, claiming instead that by dint of lineage they were the heirs to the Camarilla, the Senex (the Camarilla\u2019s ruling body), the Invictus (the eldest members of the Senex) or any number of hoary governing bodies of the Kindred past. These Kindred recognized the power and zealousness of the Sanctified, however and attributed their right to rule justly to God as well as to their blood. Most maintained strong ties and amiable relationships with their coreligionists in the Lancea+Sanctum.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T14:06:09-07:00","id":1345323,"title":"","content":"Also, the Holy Land likely wouldn't end up firmly in Lancea et Sanctum's control; most likely they're nominally holding the region, but more realistically Al-Hamasoun is actively a threat to their power and both are at one another's throats. The Christianity that the Lancea et Sanctum is important. Despite the Crusaders being Catholics, Coptics and Eastern Orthodox are still going to have stronger presences. It could also help to look in the way that minority religions like Jewish, Samaritan, and Polytheist vampires are affected; it should be noted that the Polytheists and Samaritans would likely be in much smaller cult structures and that the Jewish vampires would either have a similar cult or relatively small covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T14:46:06-07:00","id":1345331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spectre9924</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1344641-lancea-et-sanctum-in-the-crusades?p=1345323#post1345323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it should be noted that the Polytheists and Samaritans would likely be in much smaller cult structures and that the Jewish vampires would either have a similar cult or relatively small covenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is ironical, as Lancea Sanctum started as Jewish heretical small Covenant, becoming more and more Christian-like with coming years...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=873026#post873026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, RfR also stablishes that the Lancea et Sanctum was originally a jewish vsmpiric cult (the Sanctum) in the Collegia Peregrine.<br /> Around first century, the opened to small Gnostic, Christian and marginsl vampiric faith from the Empire. The Longinians (the Lancea) was one of those faiths, but it grew until finally they became the main faction of the cult and broke with the Collegia.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T15:20:02-07:00","id":1345337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1344641-lancea-et-sanctum-in-the-crusades?p=1345331#post1345331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is ironical, as Lancea Sanctum started as Jewish heretical small Covenant, becoming more and more Christian-like with coming years...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as ironical as Christianity starting as a Jewish sect, becoming more and more separate from Judaism with time.<br /> <br /> Also, it's less that the Sanctum was the origin of the Lancea et Sanctum and more that the Sanctum was co-opted by Longinians. By the time Longinians came to Rome and joined the Sanctum they had already compiled the first version of the Testament of Longinus and was firmly a daughter religion to early Christianity. The Sanctum did shed previous Jewish and Gnostic influences (mainly by converting to Longinianism or being exiled from the group), but the Longinian faith was developed from Christianity when Judaism and Christianity had already split, and primarily got recruits from Embraced Christians. And it's that early Christian-based faith that Lancea et Sanctum is ultimately based on. It is no surprise that Lancea et Sanctum treated Jews the same way that Christians did, once they broke free from the Peregrine Collegia and became an official church.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-01-2019, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T18:14:47-07:00","id":1345362,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> oh wow. I didn\u2019t know all that. Is that in Requiem for Rome?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T04:20:39-07:00","id":1345418,"title":"","content":"It's puzzled together from that one page in RfR that Wyrd talked about with the history of the Lancea et Sanctum as described in the LS covenant book. LS describes how the faith developed and such before it spread to Rome, and RfR confirms that the Testament was already written by the time the Longinians reached the Necropolis of Rome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T09:22:27-07:00","id":1345447,"title":"","content":"Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:58:19-08:00","id":1345818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1344641-lancea-et-sanctum-in-the-crusades?p=1345418#post1345418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's puzzled together from that one page in RfR that Wyrd talked about with the history of the Lancea et Sanctum as described in the LS covenant book. LS describes how the faith developed and such before it spread to Rome, and RfR confirms that the Testament was already written by the time the Longinians reached the Necropolis of Rome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Note that the Longinians reached Rome around 380, if I recall from the other thread. So the takeover was gradual and in many ways followed the fractured canonization of early Christian church materials.<br /> <br /> Given that the core notes for the Testament must have been in place by 70AD, there's a lot of wiggle room for &quot;incomplete&quot; or edited (or original!) versions to circulate in the east.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}